{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And the reason for the sin-offering</b> that the nazirite brings on the day his nazirite days are complete is not explained. According to the plain sense, it is because this man sins against his soul in completing his naziriteship, for he now withdraws from his holiness and the service of HaShem, and it would have been fitting for him to take the vow forever and to stand all his days as a nazirite and holy to his Elohim, in the manner that it says (Amos 2:11), \"And I raised up some of your sons for prophets and some of your young men for nazirites\" — Scripture equates him with a prophet, and as it is written (Numbers 6:8), \"All the days of his naziriteship he is holy to YHWH\" — and behold, he requires atonement when he turns back to defile himself with the desires of the world."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The closing phrase בתאוות העולם, \"with the desires of the world,\" refers to the nazirite's return to ordinary life after his period of consecration."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:03:01.598974517Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}